WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.300
-Our first guest is
an Oscar-winning actress

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.634
who stars in the new movie,
"Moonfall,"

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:08.467
which hits theaters and IMAX
next Friday.

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:12.200
Ladies and gentlemen,
please welcome Halle Berry!

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:15.300
Ah, come on now!

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.067
Ah, we love you!

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:18.701
We miss you!

00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:20.534
-Hi!
-Halle!

00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:22.767
-Oh, my gosh.
It's so good to be here.

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:25.334
I wish I were there,
but I'm here, but I'm there.

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:27.100
-You're there, but you're here,
but you're there.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.567
But next time, I want you here.

00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:30.801
We miss you!
-I know! Me too!

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:33.167
-But we love you.
Can you feel the audience?

00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:34.367
Can you feel the love?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:37.167
Can you feel the love?
-Yes!

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:38.200
-There's a lot of love out there
for Halle Berry.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.667
-From that good-looking
audience.

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:43.467
-We have a lot to talk about,
but first I want to ask you --

00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:45.934
you caused quite a stir
on New Year's Day,

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:48.968
and I thought this was
very funny.

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:50.667
I just want to know the story
behind it,

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:52.734
'cause I think even Questlove --

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:54.367
-First of all, yeah.

00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:56.400
This was not supposed to happen
like this.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.334
First of all, Jimmy --
-Okay, okay, okay.

00:00:58.334 --> 00:01:01.033
-I was with my boyfriend.
We were on an island.

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:03.968
We had copious amounts of drinks
at the bar.

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:05.501
-Yes, which one does
at an island.

00:01:05.501 --> 00:01:08.067
-We're trying to make it
back to our room,

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.567
and we passed
this little chapel.

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:11.300
And we think,
"Oh, let's go in here.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.334
Let's see what's inside here."

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:14.100
So, we go in
and while we're in there,

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:17.000
we get the crazy idea, we're
thinking, "Let's fool his mom.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.234
Let's take a photo of us
and send it to her and say,

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:22.400
'Guess what, we got married,'
and then say 'Not!'" Okay?

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.067
So we took the photo and then
after we saw how good the photo

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:28.834
came out, we said, "Let's play
this joke on everybody --

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:30.501
on our friends
on Instagram too.

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:34.200
Let's post it
and then let's swipe over

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:38.601
and tell them it's official,
swipe, it's 2022, right?"

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:40.000
That's how we thought
it would play

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.267
and that everybody
would be like,

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.334
"Oh, good one, Halle,
good one, Van."

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:46.834
But instead, within five minutes

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:49.667
we got all of
these congratulations,

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:52.801
from like Ava DuVernay
and The Rock.

00:01:52.801 --> 00:01:53.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:56.901
-Like genuine congratulations.

00:01:56.901 --> 00:01:58.501
Here's the joke.

00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:01.801
So you put, "It's official."
Right?

00:02:01.801 --> 00:02:03.501
Even Questlove put, "Wow."

00:02:03.501 --> 00:02:06.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:09.067
The Rock!
No, no, no, you don't --

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:11.534
Now you know the joke's not
a joke when The Rock says,

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:12.701
"Congratulations."

00:02:12.701 --> 00:02:13.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:15.234
"Congrats, you two, beautiful."

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:17.367
And you're like, "Oh,"
but here when you swipe over,

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:20.667
this was the joke --
"It's official.

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:23.634
It's 2022, y'all."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:26.467
I think it's funny,
but no one --

00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:29.501
-Nobody got it.
-No one swiped.

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:32.100
-Jimmy, after like 20 minutes
went by,

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.067
we were like,
"We are such [bleep].

00:02:34.067 --> 00:02:35.934
Everybody believes this.

00:02:35.934 --> 00:02:38.334
We're [bleep].
How could we do this?"

00:02:38.334 --> 00:02:39.934
-"We don't mean to do that.

00:02:39.934 --> 00:02:41.834
-So many people don't swipe.

00:02:41.834 --> 00:02:43.634
I didn't know
that people don't swipe.

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:45.701
Now I'm never doing swipes
ever again

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:47.334
'cause I know nobody
looks at the [bleep]

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:48.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:51.167
[ Rim shot ]

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:54.234
-I want to congratulate you, of
course, not for getting married,

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:57.601
but your directorial debut,
"Bruised."

00:02:57.601 --> 00:03:00.901
By the way, I was in shock
to see you looking like that.

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:03.667
[ Applause ]
Great movie.

00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:05.634
It became the number-one movie
on Netflix.

00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:07.234
Not too shabby, huh?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:07.234 --> 00:03:11.801
-Thank you.
-Directorial debut.

00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:14.133
And the soundtrack is great too.

00:03:14.133 --> 00:03:17.334
I do know "Automatic Woman"
by H.E.R.

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:19.300
is in Oscar contention.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.734
It's a great, great, great song.

00:03:20.734 --> 00:03:24.367
-Yes, it's on the short list.
Like, who knew? Who knew?

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:26.300
-It's great,
but oh, my, she's fantastic.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.400
-Yeah, we're excited for that.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:34.000
-Will there be more Halle Berry
being a director?

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.267
-I hope so. I think so.

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:38.133
I certainly know
I have a lot to say.

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:40.467
And being a black woman,
I think that's the white space.

00:03:40.467 --> 00:03:42.868
We need to tell more of our
stories from our point of view.

00:03:42.868 --> 00:03:45.367
So I definitely hope so.

00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:48.367
-Yeah. Would you direct and act
again in the same thing?

00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:50.701
-No. No.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.701 --> 00:03:52.100
I'm one and done with that.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.434
That was a lot of
a lot of a lot.

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:57.000
-It's a lot of work.
-No. It was a lot.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.534
I will never do that again. No.

00:03:59.534 --> 00:04:02.567
-I learned something new
about you today.

00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:06.133
Someone around the office
told me that the first time

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:10.934
you got your taste of performing
was doing sketch comedy.

00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:13.367
Is that true?
You were at Second City?

00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:17.133
-I did. I wasn't trying to do
that though.

00:04:17.133 --> 00:04:19.234
I was just there
trying to make friends.

00:04:19.234 --> 00:04:21.667
I had moved to Chicago.
I was all by myself,

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:24.701
and I had heard that that was
a good place to meet people.

00:04:24.701 --> 00:04:29.534
So I went there, signed up, and
yeah, that's where I started.

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:31.334
And one of the teachers there
said to me,

00:04:31.334 --> 00:04:32.901
"You know, have you ever thought
about acting?"

00:04:32.901 --> 00:04:34.200
I said, "No, never."

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.000
He said,
"Well, I think you should.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.601
I think you have
some natural talent,

00:04:37.601 --> 00:04:38.801
some pretty good timing.

00:04:38.801 --> 00:04:41.234
You should give this a try."

00:04:41.234 --> 00:04:43.634
-I don't think many people talk
about that and, like,

00:04:43.634 --> 00:04:47.133
you don't have to go to
these improv classes to be

00:04:47.133 --> 00:04:49.300
on "Saturday Night Live"
or be --

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:53.400
but it's just fun to be
a funnier person.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.033
And just go and you meet
funny people

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:56.801
that also want to be funny,
so yeah, you get to hang out.

00:04:56.801 --> 00:04:58.801
-You do. And people that are
silly and free,

00:04:58.801 --> 00:04:59.968
that's what I got from it.

00:04:59.968 --> 00:05:01.968
Even the people
that weren't that funny --

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:03.501
I probably was one of them.

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:07.133
But you have the ability
to just be free, you know?

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:09.434
No restrictions.

00:05:09.434 --> 00:05:12.901
And you can say whatever
you want to say and flop.

00:05:12.901 --> 00:05:15.000
You can do --
You know, it can be amazing.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.467
It could suck.
It doesn't matter.

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:19.100
It's just about being free,
and I love that.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.534
-Congrats on "Moonfall,"
by the way.

00:05:20.534 --> 00:05:23.501
I just love even the title
before I saw the movie.

00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:26.367
I just thought It sounds like
a great movie -- "Moonfall."

00:05:26.367 --> 00:05:29.434
But this is big.
It is action-packed.

00:05:29.434 --> 00:05:32.667
I mentioned earlier it's in
theaters, but it's also in IMAX,

00:05:32.667 --> 00:05:34.467
which, man,
there's nothing like that.

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:38.567
If you see a giant action,
beautiful movie in IMAX,

00:05:38.567 --> 00:05:40.267
it's like, "Ah."

00:05:40.267 --> 00:05:43.000
-This is a perfect movie
for IMAX.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.434
I mean, you want to see
the moon, you know,

00:05:45.434 --> 00:05:47.133
coming at you in IMAX.

00:05:47.133 --> 00:05:49.167
-Yeah, exactly right, yeah.

00:05:49.167 --> 00:05:51.868
How do we set it up
for everyone, "Moonfall"?

00:05:51.868 --> 00:05:53.300
-Well, this is a story about --

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:57.133
I play a woman who used to be
an astronaut.

00:05:57.133 --> 00:06:03.834
She's now working sort of
in the offices now of NASA.

00:06:03.834 --> 00:06:08.334
And her old partner comes to her
and tells her that

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:10.767
he's figured out
a big, huge problem

00:06:10.767 --> 00:06:13.534
that Earth is going to have,
and that is that the moon

00:06:13.534 --> 00:06:17.100
is off its axis and it's going
to plummet into Earth,

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.534
and so he and I have to get
together and we have to

00:06:19.534 --> 00:06:23.601
figure out a way to save Earth
by stopping the moon.

00:06:23.601 --> 00:06:25.934
-That's exactly right. Come on!
That's what I'm talking about!

00:06:25.934 --> 00:06:28.234
-You know, something easy like
that.

00:06:28.234 --> 00:06:30.367
-Come on!
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:30.367 --> 00:06:32.334
Here's Halle Berry
in "Moonfall."

00:06:32.334 --> 00:06:33.701
Take a look at this.

00:06:33.701 --> 00:06:36.300
-Don't argue.
Just pack your stuff.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:39.133
We're leaving.

00:06:39.133 --> 00:06:40.734
-So you're just going to quit?

00:06:40.734 --> 00:06:41.868
-What do you want me to do?

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:43.100
-I want you to help us
figure out

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.968
what the hell this thing is
so we can beat it.

00:06:44.968 --> 00:06:46.367
-We're not equipped for that.

00:06:46.367 --> 00:06:48.234
You've seen what
we're up against.

00:06:48.234 --> 00:06:50.934
You've been gunning for my job
for a while, Fowler.

00:06:50.934 --> 00:06:52.901
Congrats. It's yours.

00:06:52.901 --> 00:06:54.234
-What are you not telling me?

00:06:54.234 --> 00:06:55.801
You've got Q clearance.

00:06:55.801 --> 00:06:57.767
The hole is in the Mare Crisium.

00:06:57.767 --> 00:06:59.834
That's what the Harper hearings
were all about.

00:06:59.834 --> 00:07:03.400
-You should pay a visit to
Holdenfield.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:04.901
Here's your clearance.

00:07:09.868 --> 00:07:12.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Mm-hmm! Yeah!

00:07:12.934 --> 00:07:15.934
More with Halle Berry when
we come back, everybody.

00:07:15.934 --> 00:07:17.634
We're going to do something fun.
Come on back.

